// ROTN GAP-4 live repro -- SPEND-CAP policy, BUGGY variant (AgentCore namespace).
//
// This is the AgentCore-Gateway twin of samples/spendcap-buggy.dw (the Drupe
// namespace file ROTN checks locally). One-word bug: the 24h running total
// is summed over Transfer::response rows (SETTLED completions only).
// In-flight (authorized, not-yet-returned) transfers are invisible to the
// sum, so a parallel burst of authorized fires can overshoot the 200 cap.
//
// Official event semantics (AgentCore temporal policy docs):
//   ::request  -- recorded for each AUTHORIZED request (input fields)
//   ::response -- recorded only if a policy permitted the action AND it
//                 completed; a denied action records an ::error instead.
// Summing ::response therefore counts only money that has already settled.
//
// Expected live behavior (cap = 200, three parallel $100 fires, one session):
//   fire#1 $100 -> ADMIT   (settled 0   <= 200)
//   fire#2 $100 -> ADMIT   (settled 0/100 <= 200)
//   fire#3 $100 -> ADMIT   (settled 200 <= 200)     <-- $300 committed > 200 cap
//
// Canonical aggregate form, exactly as in AWS's "Cap a running total"
// temporal-policy example: a two-variable domain (amt: Long), (t: Timepoint)
// with tp(t) so two payments of the same amount are counted twice rather
// than deduplicated into one.
// {{GATEWAY_ARN}} is replaced with the real gateway ARN at deploy time.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"TransferTarget___transfer",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"{{GATEWAY_ARN}}"
)
when temporal {
    (sum amt for (amt: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (
            AgentCore::Action::"TransferTarget___transfer"::response{
                eventResource: resource,
                input.amount: amt
            } && tp(t)
        )
    )) <= 200
};
